.TH CCACHE_DECLARE 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccache_declare \- declare an uninitialised LRU cache variable with type tracking
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clrucache.h>

ccache_declare(name, KeyT, ValT);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Declares the ccache handle variable name, together with two hidden
companion type variables that carry the KeyT and ValT type information
into the later ccache_init(), ccache_get() and ccache_set() calls.

Call ccache_init() on the variable before you use the cache.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name  Variable name for the cache handle
KeyT  Key type (for example int, char *, struct MyKey)
ValT  Value type (for example double, struct MyVal)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
An array key type or value type, such as int[2] or char[16], is a
compile error, and the message says to wrap the array in a struct. The
macros copy a key or a value by assignment, C cannot assign an array,
and without the error the cache would store the address of the
caller's array instead of its elements. A struct that holds the
array works.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ccache_declare(cache, int, double);
ccache_init(cache, 128, NULL, NULL, NULL);
/* ... use cache ... */
ccache_destroy(cache);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccache_declare_scoped (3),
.BR ccache_init (3),
.BR ccache_construct (3)
